---

<StandardPageLayout
  code={metadata.code}
  standardType={metadata.framework}
  title={metadata.title}
  description={metadata.description}
  issued={metadata.issued}
  latestAmendment={metadata.latestAmendment}
  status={metadata.status}
  summary={metadata.summary}
  bannerNotice={metadata.bannerNotice}
>
  <Fragment slot="toc">
    <PageToc
      items={[
        { id: "s1", label: "Conceptual Framework Linkage" },
        { id: "s2", label: "Scope" },
        { id: "s3", label: "The General Rule — Measurement at Fair Value" },
        { id: "s4", label: "Exception One — Lack of Commercial Substance" },
        { id: "s5", label: "Exception Two — Fair Value Not Reliably Measurable" },
        { id: "s6", label: "Exception Three — Exchanges to Facilitate Sales to Third Parties" },
        { id: "s7", label: "Exception Four — Non-Reciprocal Transfers to Owners" },
        { id: "s8", label: "The Commercial Substance Test" },
        { id: "s9", label: "Worked Example — an Exchange With Commercial Substance" },
        { id: "s10", label: "Worked Example — an Exchange Lacking Commercial Substance" },
        { id: "s11", label: "Disclosure Requirements" },
        { id: "s12", label: "Critical Judgments &amp; Estimates" },
        { id: "s13", label: "Relationship to IAS 16's Commercial Substance Test" },
        { id: "s14", label: "Statement Mapping" },
        { id: "s15", label: "Related Standards" },
        { id: "s16", label: "Glossary" }
      ]}
    />
  </Fragment>
  <div class="wrap">



<div class="section-header" id="s1"><span class="num">1</span><h2>Conceptual Framework Linkage</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
<div class="grid">
<div class="card ci span2"><div class="ctitle ci">Measuring exchanges that do not involve cash</div><div class="principle">ASPE Section 3831 governs the MEASUREMENT of NON-monetary transactions — EXCHANGES of ASSETS, liabilities, OR services THAT do NOT primarily INVOLVE monetary CONSIDERATION (e.g. BARTER arrangements, or EXCHANGES of ONE productive ASSET for ANOTHER). THE GENERAL rule is FAIR value MEASUREMENT, SUBJECT to SPECIFIC exceptions DEFAULTING instead to CARRYING amount (Sections 4–7).</div>
</div>
</div>

<div class="section-header" id="s2"><span class="num">2</span><h2>Scope</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
<div class="grid">
<div class="card cw span2"><div class="ctitle cw">Exchanges of non-monetary assets, liabilities, or services</div><div class="principle">This Section applies to TRANSACTIONS in WHICH an ENTERPRISE exchanges NON-monetary assets, LIABILITIES, or SERVICES for OTHER non-MONETARY assets, LIABILITIES, or SERVICES, WITH little OR no MONETARY consideration INVOLVED.</div>
</div>
</div>

<div class="section-header" id="s3"><span class="num">3</span><h2>The General Rule — Measurement at Fair Value</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
<div class="grid">
<div class="card cd span2"><div class="ctitle cd">Recognizing a gain or loss on exchange</div><div class="text-supporting">AS a GENERAL rule, a NON-monetary transaction is MEASURED at the FAIR value OF the asset(s) GIVEN up, OR the asset(s) RECEIVED, WHICHEVER is MORE reliably MEASURABLE — RECOGNIZING a GAIN or LOSS for the DIFFERENCE between the FAIR value and the CARRYING amount of the ASSET given UP.</div>
</div>
</div>

<div class="section-header" id="s4"><span class="num">4</span><h2>Exception One — Lack of Commercial Substance</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
<div class="grid">
<div class="card cs span2"><div class="ctitle cs">No meaningful change in future cash flows</div><div class="text-supporting">WHERE a TRANSACTION lacks COMMERCIAL substance (Section 8), it IS measured AT the CARRYING amount OF the asset GIVEN up, RATHER than FAIR value — NO gain OR loss is RECOGNIZED, GIVEN the ENTERPRISE'S economic POSITION has NOT genuinely CHANGED as a RESULT of the EXCHANGE.</div>
</div>
</div>

<div class="section-header" id="s5"><span class="num">5</span><h2>Exception Two — Fair Value Not Reliably Measurable</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
<div class="grid">
<div class="card cd span2"><div class="ctitle cd">Carrying amount used where no reliable fair value exists</div><div class="text-supporting">WHERE the FAIR value of NEITHER the asset GIVEN up NOR the ASSET received CAN be reliably MEASURED, the TRANSACTION is MEASURED at CARRYING amount INSTEAD — GIVEN there IS no RELIABLE basis for RECOGNIZING a GAIN or LOSS.</div>
</div>
</div>

<div class="section-header" id="s6"><span class="num">6</span><h2>Exception Three — Exchanges to Facilitate Sales to Third Parties</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
<div class="grid">
<div class="card cw span2"><div class="ctitle cw">Inventory swaps between competitors, filling regional gaps</div><div class="text-supporting">WHERE an ENTERPRISE exchanges a PRODUCT or PROPERTY held FOR sale in the ORDINARY course OF business FOR a SIMILAR product OR property TO be sold WITHIN the SAME line OF business — SOLELY to FACILITATE sales TO customers OTHER than the PARTIES to the EXCHANGE (a COMMON practice AMONG competitors FILLING regional SUPPLY gaps) — the TRANSACTION is MEASURED at CARRYING amount, NOT fair VALUE, SINCE no GENUINE earnings PROCESS has BEEN completed.</div>
</div>
</div>

<div class="section-header" id="s7"><span class="num">7</span><h2>Exception Four — Non-Reciprocal Transfers to Owners</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
<div class="grid">
<div class="card cd span2"><div class="ctitle cd">Spin-offs and similar restructuring transactions</div><div class="text-supporting">A NON-monetary, non-RECIPROCAL transfer TO owners (e.g. a SPIN-off, or OTHER form of CORPORATE restructuring OR liquidation) is MEASURED at CARRYING amount — REFLECTING that SUCH transactions ARE fundamentally EQUITY distributions, RATHER than ARM'S-length exchanges GIVING rise TO a genuine GAIN or LOSS.</div>
</div>
</div>

<div class="section-header" id="s8"><span class="num">8</span><h2>The Commercial Substance Test</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
<div class="grid">
<div class="card cw span2"><div class="ctitle cw">Does the transaction genuinely change future cash flows?</div><div class="text-supporting">A TRANSACTION has COMMERCIAL substance WHERE the ENTERPRISE'S future CASH flows are EXPECTED to CHANGE significantly AS a RESULT of the EXCHANGE — EITHER in TERMS of RISK, timing, OR amount — CONCEPTUALLY similar TO the COMMERCIAL substance test IAS 16 applies SPECIFICALLY to EXCHANGES of PROPERTY, plant, AND equipment (see the COMPANION Section 13 comparison), THOUGH ASPE'S own Section 3831 APPLIES this test MORE broadly, to ALL non-monetary TRANSACTIONS rather THAN PP&amp;E exchanges alone.</div>
</div>
</div>

<div class="section-header" id="s9"><span class="num">9</span><h2>Worked Example — an Exchange With Commercial Substance</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
<div class="grid">
<div class="card cw span2"><div class="ctitle cw">A genuine change in future cash flows, recognized at fair value</div>
<div class="worked" style="margin-bottom:0;"><div class="wk-title">Example: Trading specialized equipment for a delivery vehicle fleet</div><div class="wk-body">A manufacturing company exchanges specialized production equipment (carrying amount $400,000, fair value $550,000) for a fleet of delivery vehicles (fair value $550,000), fundamentally changing its future operating cash flow profile from production to distribution activities.</div><div class="wk-answer">GIVEN the TRANSACTION genuinely CHANGES the COMPANY'S future CASH flows, it HAS commercial SUBSTANCE — the COMPANY recognizes the VEHICLE fleet AT its $550,000 FAIR value, RECOGNIZING a $550,000 − $400,000 = <strong>$150,000</strong> gain ON the exchange.</div></div>
</div>
</div>

<div class="section-header" id="s10"><span class="num">10</span><h2>Worked Example — an Exchange Lacking Commercial Substance</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
<div class="grid">
<div class="card ci span2"><div class="ctitle ci">No meaningful change in economic position, no gain recognized</div>
<div class="worked" style="margin-bottom:0;"><div class="wk-title">Example: Swapping nearly identical delivery trucks</div><div class="wk-body">A logistics company exchanges one delivery truck (carrying amount $45,000, fair value $52,000) with another logistics company for an essentially identical truck (fair value $52,000), used in the exact same capacity, with no meaningful change to expected future cash flows.</div><div class="wk-answer">GIVEN the TRANSACTION lacks GENUINE commercial SUBSTANCE, the COMPANY records the NEW truck at the CARRYING amount OF the OLD truck ($45,000) — <strong>NO gain</strong> is RECOGNIZED, DESPITE the $52,000 fair VALUE of BOTH trucks.</div></div>
</div>
</div>

<div class="section-header" id="s11"><span class="num">11</span><h2>Disclosure Requirements</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
<div class="grid">
<div class="card cd span2"><div class="ctitle cd">What Section 3831 requires</div><div class="check-list"><span>Nature and measurement basis of significant non-monetary transactions during the period</span><span>Amount of any gain or loss recognized, and how fair value was determined</span></div>
</div>
</div>

<div class="section-header" id="s12"><span class="num">12</span><h2>Critical Judgments &amp; Estimates</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
<div class="grid">
<div class="card cn span2"><div class="ctitle cn">Where judgment matters most</div>
<div class="two-col"><div><div class="elabel">SIGNIFICANT JUDGMENTS</div><div class="dot-list"><span>Whether a transaction genuinely has commercial substance</span><span>Whether fair value can be reliably measured for either asset in the exchange</span></div></div>
<div><div class="elabel">SIGNIFICANT ESTIMATES</div><div class="dot-list"><span>Fair value of the assets exchanged, where reliably measurable</span></div></div></div>
</div>
</div>

<div class="section-header" id="s13"><span class="num">13</span><h2>Relationship to IAS 16's Commercial Substance Test</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
<div class="grid">
<div class="card ci span2"><div class="ctitle ci">Comparison — ASPE Section 3831 vs IAS 16</div>
<div class="td-table"><div class="th" style="grid-template-columns:1.2fr 1.2fr 1.2fr;"><span>Feature</span><span style="color:var(--color-text-warning);">ASPE Section 3831</span><span style="color:var(--color-text-info);">IAS 16</span></div>
<div class="tr" style="grid-template-columns:1.2fr 1.2fr 1.2fr;"><span>Scope of commercial substance test</span><span>ALL non-monetary transactions</span><span>PP&E exchanges specifically</span></div>
<div class="tr alt" style="grid-template-columns:1.2fr 1.2fr 1.2fr;"><span>Core test</span><span>Expected significant change in future cash flows</span><span>Same conceptual test — converged</span></div>
</div>
<div class="note">CONCEPTUALLY closely CONVERGED — the CORE commercial-SUBSTANCE reasoning IS shared, BUT ASPE gives IT a BROADER, standalone STANDARD covering ALL non-monetary TRANSACTIONS, RATHER than a NARROWER PP&amp;E-specific application.</div>
</div>
</div>

<div class="section-header" id="s14"><span class="num">14</span><h2>Statement Mapping</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
<div class="grid">
<div class="card cs span2"><div class="ctitle cs">Where every non-monetary transaction lands</div>
<div class="td-table"><div class="th" style="grid-template-columns:1.6fr 1fr 1.4fr;"><span>Event</span><span>Statement(s) affected</span><span>Notes</span></div>
<div class="tr" style="grid-template-columns:1.6fr 1fr 1.4fr;"><span>Exchange with commercial substance</span><span><span class="badge bs">BS</span> <span class="badge is">IS</span></span><span>Gain or loss recognized at fair value</span></div>
<div class="tr alt" style="grid-template-columns:1.6fr 1fr 1.4fr;"><span>Exchange lacking commercial substance</span><span><span class="badge bs">BS</span></span><span>Carried forward at existing carrying amount, no gain recognized</span></div>
</div>
</div>
</div>

<div class="section-header" id="s15"><span class="num">15</span><h2>Related Standards</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
<div class="grid">
<div class="card cd span2"><div class="ctitle cd">Cross-reference map</div>
<div class="td-table"><div class="th" style="grid-template-columns:0.8fr 2fr;"><span>Section</span><span>Connection</span></div>
<div class="tr" style="grid-template-columns:0.8fr 2fr;"><span>Section 3061</span><span>Property, Plant and Equipment — supplies the initial measurement basis for assets received in a qualifying non-monetary exchange</span></div>
</div>
</div>
</div>

<div class="section-header" id="s16"><span class="num">16</span><h2>Quick-Reference Glossary</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
<div class="grid">
<div class="card cn span2">
<div class="glossary-item"><div class="glossary-term">Commercial substance</div><div class="glossary-def">A characteristic of a transaction where the enterprise's future cash flows are expected to change significantly as a result of the exchange.</div></div>
<div class="glossary-item" style="border-bottom:none;"><div class="glossary-term">Non-monetary transaction</div><div class="glossary-def">An exchange of assets, liabilities, or services involving little or no monetary consideration.</div></div>
</div>
</div>

<div class="legend"><div class="ltitle">Financial statement key (ASPE terminology)</div><div class="lrow"><div class="litem"><span class="badge bs">BS</span> Balance Sheet </div><div class="litem"><span class="badge is">IS</span> Income Statement </div><div class="litem"><span class="badge sre">SRE</span> Statement of Retained Earnings / Statement of Changes in Equity </div><div class="litem"><span class="badge scf">SCF</span> Cash Flow Statement</div></div></div>


</div>
  <section id="history">
    <HistoryTimeline items={history.aspe3831 || []} />
  </section>
</StandardPageLayout>
